.TH OPTIMIZE:UX 1 "August 2026" "SPP CLI" "SPP Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
optimize:ux \- Pre-compile SPP-UX templates Ahead-Of-Time (AOT)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php optimize:ux
[\fI--app=AppName\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SPP-UX operates in a zero-build-step environment. By default, SPP-UX parses tagged template literals (html`...`) using Regex and document.createTreeWalker directly in the browser on the first mount. 
The \fBoptimize:ux\fR command statically analyzes .js files, extracts the template strings, and computes fine-grained PartDescriptor metadata on the server. It writes this to a globally available JS cache, allowing the client browser to skip the JIT parsing phase entirely, achieving boot speeds comparable to Vue 3.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-app=\fR\fIAppName\fR
Specify the application directory to scan in addition to the core framework components. Defaults to 'default'.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
- Scans spp/modules/spp/drishyam/js/ and src/<AppName>/ for .js files.
- Employs Regex to extract html template strings.
- Leverages PHP's DOMDocument and DOMXPath to compute accurate TreeWalker path metadata.
- Writes the compiled cache to public/sppux-cache.js.
.SH AUTHOR
SPP Framework Team
